he pulls me over to the side of the  driveway he then states he wanted to  taze me if he had a Taser and would have  shot and killed me if he had drawn his  weapon and he would have been fully  justified in killing me ever since I was  a little child my parents have instilled  in me a love for the values that the  United States holds dear my parents came  to the United States from brutal  military dictatorship and they chose the  United States because of our  Constitution Nicolas Aquino was born and  raised in the United States after his  family fled Paraguay  he says his understanding of his  family's difficult past made him want to  give back for the freedoms the u.s.  provided that is one of many factors in  in terms of why I wanted to serve this  country was so that I could uphold those  ideals that I could fight that I could  give back to the community and make sure  that they keep those freedoms when I was  really little probably about 3 I went to  my first Air Show I've always loved the  Air Force  I remember just wanting to be a part of  this country and serving it Aquino  attends the Naval Postgraduate School in  Monterey California and in many ways has  become quite the poster child for the  military so when he found out there was  a warrant out for his arrest he was  shocked  I never was arrested charged cited  booked nothing I've never even had to  had a ticket he found out he was being  charged with resisting arrest during an  incident that happened in December of  2013 an incident in which he believes he  was the victim one of akeno's neighbors  had reported seeing a suspicious person  at akeno's address aquino had been  living there for a few months but the  neighbor was rarely around and didn't  recognize him  sheriff's deputy ivan Rodriguez followed  up on the call and checked out the  residents but Aquino said the officer  didn't provide any identification when  he went out to greet him there are  plenty of police impersonators out there  a badge  online cost 60 bucks to get so my  question to him was excute excuse me who  are you  and why you're here he said he was  investigating suspicious activity in the  area I asked him am I being detained  he said yes so I was like okay my name  is Nicolas Aquino I live right here how  long am I being detained  for what are the charges and do you have  a warrant everything that Nicolas was  doing to me is sort of like textbook  like okay I'm going to be respectful I'm  going to answer questions but I'm also  going to insist that you answer  questions for me because I am within my  rights on my property to ask these  questions akeno's lawyer Steven liner  says that nothing Nicolas did suggested  aggression and the arrest report agrees  the officer though he couldn't be  reached for comment wrote in the report  that the male looked to have a normal to  slightly nervous demeanor but did not  immediately seem confrontational or  aggressive but that he later asked in a  confrontational tone if he was being  detained  the officer apparent he appears to have  been offended at the idea that a citizen  would question his authority at the  officers request aquino showed his  military ID and other forms of  identification but the officer was still  unconvinced and moved to physically  detain him he just grabbed my wrist  without any warning without provocation  put me in a front headlock choke the  technical term is a front guillotine  slam my head into the ground so  currently I still have fluid buildup in  in the back of my right ear right head  contusion both arms abrasions and  contusions on the elbows knees hip right  hip using force should have been the  last resort unless there was some reason  to believe that Nicolas was doing  something that was  you know harm him at that moment and  there was nothing that he was doing that  would cause that eventually Aquino was  able to convince the officer that he did  in fact live there the officer did not  apologize he pulls me over 